<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>KL divergence on the validation set of Regmix for vanilla KD vs. TAD. The <math id="S1.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> axis shows training progress in terms of the number of tokens, and the <math id="S1.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> axis shows held-out KL between the student and teacher. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Tail-Aware Distillation</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is the simplex of token probabilities produced by a language model (e.g., <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> for the student and <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> for the teacher), then the standard distillation loss of a causal model has the following form for a sequence of length <math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{KD}=\sum_{t=1}^{N}\mathcal{L}_{CLM}(t;\mathcal{P}^{S})+\mathcal{D}_{KL}(t;\mathcal{P}^{T},\mathcal{P}^{S})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{KD}=\sum_{t=1}^{N}\mathcal{L}_{CLM}(t;\mathcal{P}^{S})+\mathcal{D}_{KL}(t;\mathcal{P}^{T},\mathcal{P}^{S})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{CLM}(t;\mathcal{P}^{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{CLM}(t;\mathcal{P}^{S})</annotation></semantics></math> is the causal language modeling (CLM) loss of the student, and <math id="S2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{KL}(t;\mathcal{P}^{T},\mathcal{P}^{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{KL}(t;\mathcal{P}^{T},\mathcal{P}^{S})</annotation></semantics></math> is the KL divergence between the teacher and the student for the token <math id="S2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="S2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> In our method, we focus on the teacher’s next-token probabilities when we input a sequence. With some abuse of notation, if <math id="S2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}=\max_{v\in\mathcal{V}}[\{p^{T}_{1},p^{T}_{2},\dots p^{T}_{v}\dots\}\setminus\{\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}=\max_{v\in\mathcal{V}}[\{p^{T}_{1},p^{T}_{2},\dots p^{T}_{v}\dots\}\setminus\{\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>th maximum of all the token probabilities for a vocabulary <math id="S2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can split the KL divergence between the top-<math id="S2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and the rest as,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{KL}\left(\mathcal{P}^{T}\|\mathcal{P}^{S}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{KL}\left(\mathcal{P}^{T}\|\mathcal{P}^{S}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{KL}\left(p^{T}\|p^{S}\right)_{p^{T}\in\{{\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}}}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{KL}\left(p^{T}\|p^{S}\right)_{p^{T}\in\{{\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}}}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\phantom{ABCDEFGH}\alpha^{T}_{K}\mathcal{D}_{KL}\big(\tilde{p}^{T}\|\tilde{p}^{S}\big)_{p^{T}\notin\{{\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∉</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phantom{ABCDEFGH}\alpha^{T}_{K}\mathcal{D}_{KL}\big(\tilde{p}^{T}\|\tilde{p}^{S}\big)_{p^{T}\notin\{{\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ =" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ =</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{KL_{1}}+\alpha^{T}_{K}\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{KL_{1}}+\alpha^{T}_{K}\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Here <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of top-<math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> teacher probabilities, and <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{T}_{K}=1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{T}_{K}=1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the non-top-<math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> or the tail probability mass of the teacher. <math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{KL_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{KL_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the KL divergence associated with them (i.e., the modes), including a <math id="S2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K+1)</annotation></semantics></math>st term for probabilities <math id="S2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Whereas, <math id="S2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the KL Divergence for the rest, i.e., the tail, involving <math id="S2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|-K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|-K</annotation></semantics></math> terms. The terms <math id="S2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the normalized teacher (or student) probabilities for the rest, i.e., <math id="S2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}^{T}=p^{T}/(1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}^{T}=p^{T}/(1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, since the sum of the non-top-<math id="S2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> probabilities is
<math id="S2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that even if the non-top-<math id="S2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> probabilities (<math id="S2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{T}\notin\{{\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∉</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{T}\notin\{{\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}}</annotation></semantics></math>) are close to zero, their normalized values (<math id="S2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) are not. Therefore, <math id="S2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-trivially different from zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Observe that if the probability distribution is skewed towards the modes, i.e., top-<math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> token probabilities and has a thin tail, <math id="S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is very high, and the contribution of <math id="S2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> to the KL divergence is very low.
To mitigate this, we can multiply the second term by a hyperparameter <math id="S2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding the two-term loss
<math id="S2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{KL_{1}}+\beta\alpha^{T}_{k}\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{KL_{1}}+\beta\alpha^{T}_{k}\mathcal{D}_{KL_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this form, we recover the exact KL Divergence for <math id="S2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the loss requires <math id="S2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Setting the value of <math id="S2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> becomes quite difficult, and the loss does not converge. We overcome this issue by sequence-level normalization. For the stochastic form of training, we use a mini-batch of sequences, and every token in a sequence has a different value of <math id="S2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p^{T}_{1},p^{T}_{2}\dots,p^{T}_{v}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p^{T}_{1},p^{T}_{2}\dots,p^{T}_{v}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If a sequence has <math id="S2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, we can normalize <math id="S2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> by the mean of <math id="S2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{K}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{K}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> across all the tokens. Indexing the tokens with <math id="S2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, the final loss for a token <math id="S2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in the sequence takes the form,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{DIV}(t;\mathcal{P}^{T},\mathcal{P}^{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{DIV}(t;\mathcal{P}^{T},\mathcal{P}^{S})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={D}_{KL_{1}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={D}_{KL_{1}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\beta}{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{t=1}^{N}\alpha^{T}_{k}(t)}\alpha^{T}_{k}(t){D}_{KL_{2}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\beta}{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{t=1}^{N}\alpha^{T}_{k}(t)}\alpha^{T}_{k}(t){D}_{KL_{2}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This normalization makes the loss stable for nominal values of <math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, such as <math id="S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. This also preserves the overall shape of the teacher probability distribution, but only amplifies the tail’s contribution to the KL divergence. Finally, we add the causal language modeling (CLM) loss of the student <math id="S2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{CLM}(\mathcal{P}^{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{CLM}(\mathcal{P}^{S})</annotation></semantics></math> for every token <math id="S2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> to the divergence to constitute the final loss as,</span></p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{TAD}=\sum_{t=1}^{N}\mathcal{L}_{CLM}(t;\mathcal{P}^{S})+\mathcal{L}_{DIV}(t;\mathcal{P}^{T},\mathcal{P}^{S})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{TAD}=\sum_{t=1}^{N}\mathcal{L}_{CLM}(t;\mathcal{P}^{S})+\mathcal{L}_{DIV}(t;\mathcal{P}^{T},\mathcal{P}^{S})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We refer to the original form of KD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hinton et al., 2014</a>)</cite> as Vanilla KD, which replaces <math id="S2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DIV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DIV}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2 Tail-Aware Distillation ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> with the KL divergence. When we train by optimizing <math id="S2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DIV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">DIV</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DIV}}</annotation></semantics></math> (see <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Pretraining Distillation from Scratch ‣ 3 Experimental Details ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>), the student attains a lower held-out KL than when trained by optimizing KL itself (<a href="#S1.F1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), even though KL is the evaluation metric. We also show the variation in tail probability mass (<math id="S2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{T}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{T}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>) with <math id="S2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> across different teachers in <a href="#S2.F2" title="In 2 Tail-Aware Distillation ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Our method is motivated by decoupled knowledge distillation (DKD; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2022)</a></cite>), which was proposed for supervised classification with labeled datasets and improves accuracy on ImageNet and CIFAR-100. In contrast, language model pretraining distillation operates on unlabeled corpora, so the original DKD formulation is not well-suited to this setting. While one might treat the next token as a target label, this creates a fundamental mismatch: in classification, the target class is, by definition, correct. However, since most LMs’ pretraining corpora are undisclosed and we distill using a generic corpus, the teacher’s most probable token (i.e., <math id="S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max_{v\in\mathcal{V}}p_{v}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max_{v\in\mathcal{V}}p_{v}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) may differ from the ground-truth next token. When we study this discrepancy on the validation set of our dataset (see <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Pretraining Distillation from Scratch ‣ 3 Experimental Details ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>), we observe a mismatch rate ranging from <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="39\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">39</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">39\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="46\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">46</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">46\%</annotation></semantics></math>, depending on the teacher, with larger teachers having lower mismatch rates (<a href="#S2.F2" title="In 2 Tail-Aware Distillation ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). This mismatch creates conflicting signals between the dataset labels and teacher predictions. We therefore introduce TAD: a rank-based Top-<math id="S2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> vs. tail decoupling using a probability-mass-normalized tail KL divergence that preserves the teacher’s distributional information. TAD is not a variant of DKD: DKD’s decoupling is label-anchored (target vs. non-target), while TAD’s is rank-anchored (Top-<math id="S2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> vs. tail) and label-free. Two examples with identical values of <math id="S2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> yield the same TAD losses, but their DKD losses can be different if their labels differ.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S2.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20816v1/TopK.svg" id="S2.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/320;" width="476" height="320"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.sf1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S2.F2.sf1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Tail Probability Mass</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S2.F2.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20816v1/Mismatch.svg" id="S2.F2.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/318;" width="476" height="318"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.sf2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S2.F2.sf2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Mismatch Rate</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="S2.F2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Tail probability mass (<math id="S2.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{T}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{T}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>) against <math id="S2.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> for different teachers in the first, and the Next Token vs. Mode mismatch rate in percentage in the second plot, measured on the validation set of Regmix (see <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Pretraining Distillation from Scratch ‣ 3 Experimental Details ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>)</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Gradient Analysis</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For a token </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> in a sequence </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> of length </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, the KL Divergence loss is </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{KLD}=\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{V}|}p_{i}^{T}\log(p_{i}^{T}/p_{i}^{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{KLD}=\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{V}|}p_{i}^{T}\log(p_{i}^{T}/p_{i}^{S})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where the probabilities </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are typically produced by the softmax of the logit </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> of the final layer, the gradient has the following form. For the sake of simplicity, we omit the index </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> from the equations.</span></p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{KLD}}{\partial z_{i}}=p_{i}^{S}-p_{i}^{T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{KLD}}{\partial z_{i}}=p_{i}^{S}-p_{i}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since the top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> probabilities of the teacher, denoted </span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, are much larger than the tail probabilities (i.e., </span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}\gg p^{T}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≫</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}\gg p^{T}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for </span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[\mathcal{V}\setminus K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[\mathcal{V}\setminus K]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">), the gradients w.r.t. the logits of the top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> tokens are much greater than the those of the tail tokens’ logits. This forces the student model to focus primarily on the top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> tokens, pushing the sum of the student’s top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> probabilities close to 1, i.e., </span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≈</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For Tail-aware KD, the gradient of the loss w.r.t. the logits of the top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> probabilities remains the same as </span><a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.1 Gradient Analysis ‣ 2 Tail-Aware Distillation ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a><span id="S2.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. However, for the tail logits (</span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}:i\in[\mathcal{V}\setminus K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}:i\in[\mathcal{V}\setminus K]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">), it has the form</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{DIV}}{\partial z_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{DIV}}{\partial z_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{i}^{S}-p_{i}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{i}^{S}-p_{i}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\big(\beta(X)-1\big)\left(p^{S}_{i}\cdot\frac{1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}}{1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}}-p^{T}_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\big(\beta(X)-1\big)\left(p^{S}_{i}\cdot\frac{1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}}{1-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}}-p^{T}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(X)=\beta/(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{t=1}^{N}\alpha^{T}_{k}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(X)=\beta/(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{t=1}^{N}\alpha^{T}_{k}(t))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is defined in </span><a href="#S2.Ex6" title="In 2 Tail-Aware Distillation ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and is specific to the sequence </span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are the student probabilities corresponding to the tokens of top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> teacher probabilities. We typically set </span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(X)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> has probability terms in the denominator, making </span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(X)&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(X)&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. When </span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≈</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, the second term of </span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{z_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{DIV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∇</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{z_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{DIV}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (</span><a href="#S2.Ex8" title="In 2.1 Gradient Analysis ‣ 2 Tail-Aware Distillation ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) increases the relative weight of tail gradients, causing the tail probability of the student to rise, ensuring that </span><math id="S2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p3.2.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This mechanism ensures that the tail probability of the student will rise with each gradient step as long as the top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> probability of the student is more than the teacher’s, i.e., </span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}\geq\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}\geq\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. In this case, the gradient satisfies: </span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{z_{i}}{\mathcal{L}_{DIV}}\geq\beta(X)(p_{i}^{S}-p_{i}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∇</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{z_{i}}{\mathcal{L}_{DIV}}\geq\beta(X)(p_{i}^{S}-p_{i}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, which is stronger than the standard KL gradient. Once the top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> probability mass of the student matches the teacher’s, i.e., </span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}\approx\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}\approx\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, the gradient compensation stops. At this point, the </span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{z_{i}}{\mathcal{L}_{DIV}}\approx\beta(X)(p_{i}^{S}-p_{i}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∇</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{z_{i}}{\mathcal{L}_{DIV}}\approx\beta(X)(p_{i}^{S}-p_{i}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The fixed point of the gradient lies at </span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{S}=p_{i}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{S}=p_{i}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, same as Vanilla KD, and therefore converges to the same solution. By this stage, the student has already acquired a sufficient mass in the tail probabilities and has begun to generalize beyond the top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> tokens. On the other hand, if </span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}&lt;\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{S}_{k}&lt;\sum_{k=1}^{K}\accentset{\ast}{p}^{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, the strong gradient of top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> tokens will drive up the top-</span><math id="S2.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> probability mass of the student. This way, Tail-aware KD enables a better learning of the teacher probabilities across the entire vocabulary. The full derivation is included in the </span><a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Derivation of the Gradient ‣ Don’t Ignore the Tail: Decoupling top-𝐾 Probabilities for Efficient Language Model Distillation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S2.T1.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S2.T1.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T1.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S2.T1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:11.4pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T1.3.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Teacher/Student</span></span>
