<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S2.T1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results for Tail-aware distillation for <math id="S2.T1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=2</annotation></semantics></math> over Qwen1.5-1.8B (<span id="S2.T1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote">“Qn”</span>), for a 1.2B and 0.5B student model. The best performance for each column, and any value within <math id="S2.T1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.4</annotation></semantics></math> of it, is highlighted. CLM stands for pre-training the model with only the CLM loss, without distillation. The average relative change for the best-case TAD (<math id="S2.T1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=10</annotation></semantics></math>) is 50% to 120% better than MiniPLM.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We distill models of varying sizes, ranging from Qwen1.5 (1.8B) to Gemma-2 (9 B). We do not have access to (or require) the pretraining corpus of any of these models. MiniPLM was trained on the Pile dataset </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2020</a><span id="S3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, an extensive 825 GB collection that is no longer available due to copyrighted content. We instead use a small 20GB subsample</span><span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/sail/regmix-data-sample" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/sail/regmix-data-sample</a></span></span></span><span id="S3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> of the Regmix dataset </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024b</a><span id="S3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, containing a total of 5B tokens, that can be processed using our limited compute setting. Regmix replicates the Pile, but without copyrighted components.</span></p>
</div>
